From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the draw-done mask round trip when nothing is latched
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance, no behaviour change.

Every SDK clock query delivers a latched GX finish (glx WaitDrawDone polls the
clock until its draw-done callback runs). Without a latched finish there is
nothing to deliver, yet each query took and released the interrupt exclusion.
Check the latch first; delivery, interrupt masking and callback order are
unchanged when a finish is pending. Apply after 0069.
diff --git a/lib/gx/fifo.cpp b/lib/gx/fifo.cpp
index 16bdedf..80b818c 100644
--- a/lib/gx/fifo.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/fifo.cpp
@@ -293,6 +293,10 @@ void publish_draw_done() noexcept {
 bool service_draw_done() {
   // A background SDK yield never dispatches game callbacks on that worker.
   if (sOwner != std::this_thread::get_id()) return false;
+  // Every SDK clock query calls this. Without a latched finish there is
+  // nothing to deliver, so skip the interrupt-exclusion round trip. A finish
+  // latched after this check is delivered by the next call, as before.
+  if (!sGpuFinishPending.load(std::memory_order_acquire)) return false;
   const BOOL enabled = OSDisableInterrupts();
   struct Mask { BOOL enabled; ~Mask() { OSRestoreInterrupts(enabled); } } mask{enabled};
   if (!enabled || !sGpuFinishPending.exchange(false, std::memory_order_acq_rel)) return false;
